1. First, calculate the total distance Hannah will run:
   \[
   \text{Total distance} = \text{Number of laps} \times \text{Distance per lap} = 8 \times 0.25 \, \text{km} = 2 \, \text{km}
   \]

2. Next, calculate the total amount of water Hannah will need to drink:
   \[
   \text{Total water needed} = \text{Total distance} \times \text{Water per kilometer} = 2 \, \text{km} \times 60 \, \text{ml/km} = 120 \, \text{ml}
   \]

